Z||000000||sailordude||11-06-2001||02:01 PM||||Ok,<BR>  Come this summer I'm planning a engine swap.  I was just wondering from those of you who have made swaps what is the best engine to swap with?  What you feel are the pros and cons of your engine of choice.  Also what kind of suspension work will have to be done because of the new weight.  Also what should I be looking to spend on a the swap.  That includes everything except the price of the engine.<P>Thanks in advance for all the replies.<P>Hope to hear from you all with experience on this one.<P>Thanks,<P>Darren||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||11-06-2001||02:19 PM||||I love my Northstar...www.members.home.net/jaygrande to see it.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||11-06-2001||03:15 PM||||3.4 GM performance crate motor:<P>gobs of torque, easy to install, no need for new suspension, looks factory...<P>Price depends on what you want, The must haves are:<P>starter drill bit guide-- $50 to rent<P>88 flywheel/flex plate-- $depends<P>all factory equipment from your V6 bolts on.<P>you can use the 2.8 injectors for the crate performance because it doesnt rev up very far anyway,  could use a performance chip to take care of the lack of vacuum from the cam.<P>disconnect egr with performance chip : free<P>performance chip for 2.8: $100<P>low temp thermostat: $20<P>......................<BR>optional:<BR>3.4 upto 5.7 injectors---14 to 25 lbs/hr<BR>upgraded igniton<BR>upgraded exhaust<BR>big bore throttle body<BR>ported intake<BR>cold air intake<BR>ported polished and shaved heads<BR>high compression pistons<BR>windage tray<BR>high volume oil pump<BR>all the other 2.8 mods...<P>that should be enough to get you into the 13 sec qtr range.<p>[This message has been edited by Formula (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||11-06-2001||04:29 PM||||Depends on what you want out of the car.  A high performance machine=V8,Northstar<BR>A mod performance machine=3800s/c<BR>A good performance machine=3800 series II, HO 3.4, turbo anything.<BR>A reliable machine=crate 3.4L, 3.1L.<P>Difficulty & cost (new engines all the way)<BR>V8/Northstar   $8$$$<BR>3800 s/c  $7$$$<BR>3800 series II, HO 3.4, turbo $6$$$<BR>3.4/3.1  $4$$$<P>Other upgrades to consider brakes, suspension<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||sailordude||11-06-2001||04:43 PM||||I'm looking for something that is going to be quick off the line that is going to last a while and possibly will be able to stand up as a daily driver.  However I'll be more then happy if it will beat most imports from red light to red light.<P>Any ideas on this one?||||reg||1
Z||000005||MinnGreenGT||11-06-2001||04:55 PM||||Well, the 3.1L or 3.4L are definitely the easiest to do (just like a stock-swap).  And you can get near 200hp with it without <B>too</B> much trouble (exhuast porting, head port/polish, chip, MSD iginition, etc). That'll beat most "ricers" light-to-light (just don't let them get their turbos spooled up on the highway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  Otherwise a 3800 (S/C is preferred) can be an awsome, reliable powerplant (It'll just cost a bit more initially).  The V8 is the ultimate, much of which way you go is dependant on your budget.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||BlackStang95||11-06-2001||05:00 PM||||The best engine?  Vector W-16 Quad Turbo rated at 987 hp  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.  For a fiero swap, i think its the supercharged series 2.  ||||reg||1
