Z||000010||Spektrum-87GT||11-06-2001||06:07 PM||||wait for the new v12 northstar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>what old lar said was the best response you're going to get... although you could do a small block chevy swap for WAY below 8k if you do it yourself and go with carbs instead of fuel injection. my swap would have costed me 5k(high estimate) and i would have had a reliable 300hp engine. of course, it wasnt BRAND new, like from the dealer, but it would have been rebuilt. here's what my research came up with:<BR>v8: 5k<BR>3800 s/c: 4k(a lot of custom work needed, but i'm pretty handy, so that doenst include a kit)<BR>dohc 3.4: 4k(dont get if you want a reliable engine)<BR>3.4: 2500<P>these are what <B>I</B> came up with, but i've heard you always end up spending more than you think.<P>beat most imports red light to red light? if you've got the 2.8 with a stick, you can do that already  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||fieroX||11-06-2001||06:43 PM||||im going with the 3800 supercharged sII.  Im going to complete the swap for under $3500, thats including rebuilding the engine, transmission and the price of everything.  check out my website <A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroX.com</A>  in the future.  I will be detailing this swap to the T, but nothing has happened other than engine teardown, and nothing is on the site yet other than a logo.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
