Z||000014||lildevil||11-06-2001||08:36 PM||||I did my 3800SC conversion for around 4000 dollars. I used WestCoast Fiero for the mounts and the wire harness was done by a company out of Alabama. The rest did my self and was easy. No cutting or welding. I use the auto and the car is driven everyday with no problems. I race the car on Fridays and runs 13.2's and gets 30 miles to the gallon Highway. It'll be in the march issue of High Performance Pontiac so look for it.<P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||sailordude||11-06-2001||09:13 PM||||Is it possible to put the 3800SC with the 4 speed getrag?||||reg||1
Z||000016||fieroX||11-06-2001||09:32 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sailordude:<BR><B>Fiero X,<BR>  What did it cost to get that 3800SC rebuilt?  Are you going to with an automatic or stick shift?<P>thanks for the reply.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I paid 348.11 for new bearings rings and a full gasket set.  I paid 220 for the rods resized, pistons thermal coated for nitrous, the side skirts dry lubed, and the crankshaft micro polished.  The valve job will only cost me $100, I have a hookup.  Im doing all the port work myself.  All the assembly costs 0, I do it myself.  Im going with the 4t65e as it is matched for my engine, and my car is originally a auto.  I like manuals, but I dont want the hassle of switching over, or the computer malfunction problems.  Just check out my website over the next few months and it will develop as my project does.  Good luck!<P><p>[This message has been edited by fieroX (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
