Z||000020||sailordude||11-08-2001||12:53 AM||||Thanks for all the replies guys...but I'm still at the same point as I was before I posted this topic.  Basically my choices are the 3800, the 3.4 crate, N*'s, and the 350's.<P>But what are all the pro's and con's of these engine?  I know I want to stay with a manual trans so does that limit my choices?  I also know that I don't want to have to cut away my trunk.  Also would I be better off just modifying the heck out of my 2.8 then spending all the money and making the swap?  Any other ideas?  Is there any possible way of adding a non GM engine?<P>Well thanks again for the advice guys.  I am sortta new here, I've only been a Fiero owner since June (thanks billfredmike)and I already want more power.  <P>Well any ideas feel free to post.<P>Thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000021||87FieroGTx||11-08-2001||01:24 AM||||~~~SBC~~~<P>Power         ******(250-400hp)<BR>Reliability   ***<BR>Sound         ****<BR>Price         $8,000<BR>0-60          4.0-4.5<BR>1/4           12.5<BR>MPG           (?)(LOW)<P>~~~Northstar~~~<P>Power         ****(300hp)<BR>Reliability   ****<BR>Sound         ***<BR>Price         $9,000+<BR>0-60          (?)<BR>1/4           13.5-13.8 (slow for the $$)<BR>MPG           (?)<P>~~~3.4~~~<P>Power         ** (160hp)<BR>Reliability   ***<BR>Sound         **<BR>Price         $2500<BR>0-60          7.0<BR>1/4           14.5<BR>mpg           (?)<P>~~~3.8n/a~~~<P>Power         *** 200hp)<BR>Reliability   *****<BR>Sound         ***<BR>Price         $4,000<BR>0-60          (?)<BR>1/4           (?)<BR>MPG           30mpg<P>~~~3.8s/c~~~<P>Power         **** (260)<BR>Reliability   *****<BR>Sound         *****(S/C)<BR>Price         $5,500<BR>0-60          (?)<BR>1/4           13.3<BR>MPG           30mpg<P>I think the Best ALL AROUND engine swap is the 3.8s/c<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 87FieroGTx (edited 11-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||sqoach||11-08-2001||01:42 AM||||What's so unreliable about the 3.4? I'll be looking to swap one in when my 2.8 dies. Seems to be one of the easiest swaps, and not too expensive. And it's perfect for what I want. More kick than the stock V6.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||5
Z||000023||BlackDragon||11-08-2001||02:04 AM||||squoach, where are you getting an s/c for a 2.5? how much does it cost? pm me if you read this, im realy interested in this. thanks. <P>oh and by the way sailordude, you need to talk to archie. if you want an engine swap that will beat just about anything red light to red light, or on the highway, he can hook you up with a 10 second car. i know this is a controversial subject, but he can do it. i would personaly go with a 350 or 400 small block. if you go with an aluminum block, you will add very little weight. and a 350 is reliable if you dont supercharge it. the cons are mainly gas mileage. no matter wat the swap, the more power the less mileage. you can keep a standard transmision with any swap. even the v8, doesn't matter. archie makes a kit to bult up. you will not need to remove the trunk, it will fit. the v8 is most expensive, but you also get the most upgradeability. for example, if you put a 3800 sc in your car and later decide it is not enough power, upgrading it will be difficult, and limited to basicaly nitrous, however, if you have a v8 and later decide you want more power, that would be very easy to do. this is my 2 cents, and you will find that most (minus the people who are die hard turbo fans) will agree with me<P>------------------<BR>riced civics suck||||reg||1
Z||000024||sqoach||11-08-2001||02:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackDragon:<BR><B>squoach, where are you getting an s/c for a 2.5? how much does it cost? pm me if you read this, im realy interested in this. thanks. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That SC stands for sport coupe. I guess it is a little confusing. I wish my coupe was supercharged  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000025||87FieroGTx||11-08-2001||03:35 AM|||| Not a flame on you BlackDragon<BR> but the 3.8 has a HUGE and upcoming aftermarket!<P> Get the 3.8 supercharger and TB ported, get a underdrive pulley wala 300hp.<P> Port your heads for a 30hp gain.<P> Nice exhaust/headers/cat 20-30hp.<P> Chip 10-15hp<P> Still not enough? Get the thrasher Intercooler for $3,000 Expensive but people have reported 50-75hp<P> This is 400-450 Reliable/derivable HP!! That's way more than "I" could use in a daily driver.||||reg||1
